"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nA large cathedral in Sydney.  \nThis is the site of Australia's first Catholic church, with the foundation stone laid in 1821.  \nThe building was destroyed by fire in 1865, rebuilt, and completed in its current form in 1928.\n\nBuilt in the English Gothic style, it's an impressively large and grand structure.  \nThe exterior, constructed from Sydney sandstone, makes for a striking visual.\n\nLocated right next to Hyde Park, it's very accessible and free to enter.  \nAlong with Saint Patrick's Cathedral in Melbourne, it's considered one of Australia's most iconic cathedrals.  \nNote that visitors are required to cover their shoulders and knees when entering.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"